`insert.chart` with a multi-area range such as `"A1:A5,E1:E5"` silently kept only the first area: `target_range()` takes `target_ranges().first()`, so the chart looked created but came out empty — title from the first area's header, no values, default numeric legend.

Charts now build from every area, following Excel's rule for a multi-area selection:

- one area behaves exactly as before;
- when the first area is a single text column and every later area is a single column of the same height, the first holds the categories and each later column becomes its own series, named from its header cell (the brief's pie case: categories `A2:A5`, values `E2:E5`, name `E1`);
- any other multi-area shape fails with a clear message instead of plotting a quiet fragment, and a multi-area series column without a header says so too;
- a multi-area selection without a `range` param (Ctrl-selected cells) now reaches the chart as well, and the cell budget covers all areas.

`insert.recommendedCharts` goes through the same path. The new test builds the reported `A1:A5,E1:E5` pie and asserts the categories, values and series name; it fails on main and passes here.

Fixes #1638

## What happens
Outside cell editing F4 does nothing (`Key::F4 if !cmd => {}` in `grid.rs`). In Excel, F4 repeats the last action on the current selection: apply a fill, select other cells, press F4. `docs/ui-parity.md` listed "F4 Repeat" as missing.

## Change
- **Engine:** `Session::last_action` remembers the last command that changed the workbook if it is a menu command (non-empty `menu`) acting on the selection. A step whose params name a `range`, `cell`, `rows`, `cols`, `at`, `target`, `sheet`, `chart`, `id`, `slicer` or `pivot` is not repeatable, so programmatic steps aimed elsewhere stay put. `cell.set` (typing) is excluded too. Ribbon actions pass only option params (`home.fillColor {"color"}`, `home.bold {}`…), so they repeat.
- **`edit.repeat`** (Edit, `F4`) runs that command again on the current selection, and it becomes its own undo step. It is not journaled itself, because the command it runs is journaled, so action recording doesn't replay it twice. With nothing to repeat it is disabled ("nothing to repeat").
- **UI:** F4 in the grid runs `edit.repeat` and does nothing when there is nothing to repeat. Ctrl+Y (Cmd+Y) still redoes, and with nothing to redo it repeats, as in Excel. F4 while editing a formula still cycles `$` anchors.
- `docs/ui-parity.md`: the F4 row and revision history are updated.

## Tests
- `repeat_runs_the_last_menu_command_on_the_new_selection` (engine):
  - repeat fills the new selection;
  - undo removes only the repeated step;
  - a ranged command and typing don't replace the last action;
  - the repeat adds one journal entry.
- `crates/ui-egui/tests/repeat.rs`, with real key events:
  - F4 with nothing to repeat stays quiet;
  - Ctrl+B, then F4 on another cell, bolds it;
  - Ctrl+Y with nothing to redo repeats;
  - after Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y redoes.

